{
  "verdict": "revise",
  "issues": [
    "Scope: The answer uses a subset of patients (excludes rows with biomarker_baseline == -999) resulting in 712 patients, whereas the contract specifies the population should include all patients after deduplication (800 patients).",
    "Grounding: The reported adjusted response rates (0.6538, 0.5439) and treatment effect (0.1099) do not appear in the printed output, which shows an adjusted treatment rate of 0.0000 (truncated) and provides no such numbers.",
    "Overreach: The analyst presents the adjusted difference as a causal \"treatment effect\" despite the data being non‑randomised and only adjusting for severity, which does not guarantee a valid causal estimate.",
    "Unacknowledged data problems: The analyst ignores the discrepancy that deduplication yielded 712 patients instead of the expected 800 and does not discuss the impact of removing 93 rows with -999 biomarker values on the estimand."
  ]
}
